    <title>Prompt Injection Attacks Against Tool-Using LLM Agents:
      A Systematic Study</title>
    <summary>  We study prompt injection attacks that hijack tool-using large language model
      agents. We present a taxonomy of injection surfaces and show that indirect
      injection through retrieved documents bypasses common guardrails.
    </summary>
    <author>
      <name>Alice Zhang</name>
